# CORRIGENDUM to the retained log gen_fu_l31b_drain_corrections.log (landing 32, committed a759752).
# The retained log is NOT edited. A retained log is never reopened, so the correction lives here with its own row in
# gen_manifest.md. It answers CR-31b-L-1 and CM209-Low-3.
#
# WHAT IS WITHDRAWN. One clause of the retained log's PROVENANCE block reads, of landing 31's build:
#   "its local compile figure is 64f9aee6f60d7c84 from wit/l31a/compile.log"
# The clause is wrong twice over. Landing 31's evidence was not built in wit/l31a and its local figure is not
# 64f9aee6f60d7c84. Both halves are corrected below from the runs' own files.
#
# WHICH ROOT LANDING 31 ACTUALLY BUILT IN: dv/auto_dv/work/tb-infra/wit/l31c, whose local compile figure is
#   d34daf56c8871437.
# The attribution is not asserted, it is matched. The committed landing-31 log (gen_fu_l31_irq_drain.log) quotes five
# drain lines by run name and cycle count: seed 7 lockstep_irq_storm_nmi at 120 cycles, then the blast-radius rows
# lockstep_zc 110, ut_witness 32, boot_zc 115 and lockstep_zcmp 117. All five pairs are in wit/l31c, whose seed-7
# header reads seed=7, and the seed-7 line "17 records in 120 cycles" is in exactly ONE root of this work directory,
# measured below over all of them. wit/l31a cannot be their source: it prints no drain line at all.
#
# WHAT wit/l31a IS, since the figure is real and belongs to something. It is an earlier build of the same landing-31
# work, not a phantom: its seed-7 lockstep_irq_storm_nmi PASSES, it prints ZERO drain lines, and its own checker
# summary ends "open at the end but younger than the bound=1". So at l31a the end-of-run records-only rule had
# already been retired and the drain did not yet exist, which is why the run passes with an expectation left open and
# why it carries none of the drain lines the landing quotes. 64f9aee6f60d7c84 is l31a's figure and only l31a's.
#
# THE PRE-FIX RED IS dv/auto_dv/work/tb-infra/wit/nmi1, local compile figure f80e2c719e16b73c, seed 7. Its
# lockstep_irq_storm_nmi verdict is FAIL and it carries, verbatim, the error line the committed landing-31 log quotes
# as the false failure the landing removes. Its gate identity is the one the landing already records for the pre-fix
# build, b48479a3bc6f1d9f, which no row here changes.
#
# THE CORRECTED BUILD'S LOCAL COMPILE FIGURE, which the retained log promised and did not print: the landing-32
# sources were built out of tree in the root the MEASUREMENTS block names in full as FIX, which is
# l31fix_root/dv/auto_dv/work/tb-infra/wit/fix under the team scratchpad, local compile figure 98629b00cb34e79e.
# That is the root whose seed-7 run prints "drain: 18 records in 126 cycles (bound 17 records plus one, cap 193 ...)"
# and whose capmove3 run prints the 147-cycle drain at cap 227 under +gen_ibus_rvalid_max=6, the two lines the
# retained log quotes for the fix. Its mutant sibling is wit/mut, local figure e395bce5f2ec662b.
#
# THE ROOT CAUSE, AND IT IS GENERAL. A local compile figure is a digest of source CONTENT, so it never identifies a
# root: any two roots whose env, tb, isa and gen_tb match print the same figure. Measured below: f80e2c719e16b73c is
# printed by FOUR roots in this work directory (L25b, nmi1, peb_ecc_tag_freq_noprobe, peb2_ecc_tag_freq_noprobe),
# whose sources were the same committed state. A record that means to name a root therefore names its PATH, and the
# figure beside it is a statement about the sources, not about the directory. The withdrawn clause did the opposite:
# it read a figure off one root's compile log and attached it to another root's name.
#
# NO GATE IDENTITY CHANGES. The gate digests the landing records stand as recorded and were reproduced independently
# by the Critic in tb_l31b: landing 31 c1189fdc15a85844, landing 32 e674e6339b5bea85, the MUT-NT2 mutant root
# d02bca6ca353117f, the pre-fix build b48479a3bc6f1d9f. The gate function (gen_flow_util.filelist_digest over
# gen_rtl.f plus gen_tb.f) and the local find-digest are different functions over different input sets; only the
# local figures are corrected here.

